   "en": "Units, both land and naval, obtain their names from either a set list of names."
  },
  {
   "k": "1pwx2gn",
   "en": "Divisions Names"
  },
  {
   "k": "1k8fa3v",
   "en": "Division names are defined in ⟦0⟧ in country specific text files. The name of the file does not matter, though generally follow the following format ⟦1⟧.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "ufjs9n",
   "en": "/Hearts of Iron IV/common/units/names_divisions"
  },
  {
   "k": "fqtiv9",
   "en": "TAG_names_divisions.txt"
  },
  {
   "k": "1o6ij1h",
   "en": "Once in the file, you want to start off with the name list set in your OOB found in ⟦0⟧, for example NEP_MTN_01. You will want to follow the following formatting:",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "xc42nu",
   "en": "/Hearts of Iron IV/history/units"
  },
  {
   "k": "71d5wo",
   "en": "Namelist files seem to have a limit of ~1500 lines. Any namelists beyond that limit may not work correctly, or not appear entirely."
  },
  {
   "k": "1snd0x3",
   "en": "Naval Names"
  },
  {
   "k": "j5c5fs",
   "en": "Naval names are defined in ⟦0⟧ in country specific text files. The name of the file does not matter, though generally follow the following format ⟦1⟧.",
